-## Subtopics
-
-### [Standard Interval Tree for Isosurface Extraction](1230-standard-interval-tree-for-isosurface-extraction.md)
-Uses interval trees to cull empty space and traverse only relevant regions, differing from explicit face/edge/vertex enumeration. Choose it when scene sparsity is high and memory bandwidth is a bottleneck [G].
-
-### [Marching Cubes with Octree](1259-marching-cubes-with-octree.md)
-Applies Marching Cubes directly on an octree without explicit cross-depth traversal, risking cracks if depth mismatches are not resolved. Choose it for uniform or strictly level-aligned octrees [G].
-
-### [IsoOctree](1744-isooctree.md)
-Uses a purpose-built octree structure with different traversal and data layouts optimized for isosurface extraction. Choose it when custom memory packing and cache-aware traversal are prioritized [G].
-
-### [Wilhelms and Van Gelder Octree](2107-wilhelms-and-van-gelder-octree.md)
-Early octree method focusing on efficient traversal and memory packing using a single array representation. Choose it for legacy systems or when minimal memory overhead is critical [G].
-
-### [Ashida and Badla Octree Contouring](2117-ashida-and-badla-octree-contouring.md)
-Specialized contouring method with distinct edge-case handling and different topological guarantees. Choose it when specific contouring artifacts must be avoided in complex topologies [G].
-
-### [Unconstrained Isosurface Extraction on Arbitrary Octrees](2413-unconstrained-isosurface-extraction-on-arbitrary-octrees.md)
-Allows arbitrary octree structures without strict depth constraints, trading traversal simplicity for robustness. Choose it when the input octree cannot be guaranteed to follow a regular hierarchy [G].
-
-### [Consistent Isovertex Definition via Edge-Trees](2427-consistent-isovertex-definition-via-edge-trees.md)
-Uses edge-trees to guarantee consistent vertex definitions across the surface, preventing duplicate vertices at shared edges. Choose it when mesh watertightness and vertex sharing are mandatory [G].
-
-### [Adaptive Octree Generation with Flatness Criterion](2482-adaptive-octree-generation-with-flatness-criterion.md)
-Generates octrees based on a flatness metric rather than raw scalar thresholds, improving surface approximation quality. Choose it when geometric fidelity outweighs strict isovalue adherence [G].
-
-### [Sampled DMC](3813-sampled-dmc.md)
-Applies sampling strategies to the Dual Marching Cubes traversal pipeline to reduce computational load on smooth regions. Choose it for real-time applications where performance is prioritized over exact isosurface precision [G].
+*   **Mismatched Tree Depths:** Handled by using the ternary operator `b1 ? *b1->children()[i] : n1` to fall back to the current node `n1` when a child does not exist [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Boundary Conditions:** The recursion must handle cases where nodes at the boundary of the volume do not have all eight neighbors. The fallback mechanism ensures that missing neighbors are treated as the current node or handled appropriately to avoid segmentation faults.
 
